			<div class="content" id="post-content-1915074">
									

<p>It's a caveman duck. That's pretty funny, but I have some issues.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>In addition to the standard daily rations, SCP-1952 is to be fed 300g of electronic components every five days.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What counts as electronic components? This could use some examples given.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Should SCP-1952 become aggre<strong>s</strong>sive, it is to be sedated immediately by tranquilizer darts, which must be carried at all times by personnel.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How? Do all personnel on the site have guns? Also, make sure to spell-check.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>It is approximately 30 years old and possesses dark skin along with black hair and eyes.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I thought it was wearing a helmet. Is it like a bicycle helmet where you can see its hair poking out underneath? This might be easier if you at least described the helmet beyond its material.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1952 also possesses webbed feet similar to that of Bucephala albeola (Bufflehead), several white feathers on its back, an additional digestive system and a mechanical helmet of unknown origin permanently implanted to its skull.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's a Bufflehead? If it's a duck, put &quot;Bufflehead duck&quot; so the clarification is more clear. Also, I don't believe the correct term here is &quot;implanted&quot;. Maybe &quot;attached&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1952: …it was horrible, ok? What more do you want to know?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Ellipses shouldn't be put at the beginning of a sentence.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1952: NO! I won't talk anymore! I lost my family, my home, I was turned into a fucking monster, I can't get out of this place, I know nothing and nobody, no one cares about me, and you want me to talk MORE about it?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The capitalization of words looks really silly and unprofessional. Also, the swearing makes him sound like a whiny teenager.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

